DSL Connections

Family of technologies that provide internet access by transmitting digital data over the wires of local telephone network

Three types of DSL
    ADSL - Asymmetric; Has different download and upload speeds; Maxamizes download and minimizes upload; 4000 - 18000 ft
    SDSL - Symmetric; Works like a T1 with equal upload and download speeds; Slower speeds overall
    VDSL - Very High Bit-Rate; Has very high speeds; Down over 50 Mbps and Up over 10 Mbps; Limitation is DSLAM (Point of presence of that owned telephone company); Need to be about 4000ft from that DSLAM

    DSL declined in popularity